r spending a  lot of time with a sheet they can test  the patience somewhat I would never  discourage my daughter from going  farming despite it being hard work and  the bean days when you maybe don't want  to be doing it there's a lot of  positives in it as well and it's a great  life it's quite a nice feeling for me  knowing that you know my forefathers and  grandfather farmed this land and I'm  almost thinking that the way forward at  the moment is to go back to how things  were farmed a long time ago which which  seems odd in some respects but I think  we've got a farm in tune with nature and  we've got a farm in a way which doesn't  impact negatively upon the natural  environment around us so there's quite a  nice feeling about that but you know  that doesn't mean that I would put any  pressure on my daughter to to take it  over but if she wanted to that big  you  you
 

